 "result": "**Decorator:** `@needs_app_scope`, defined at `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It loads the app and pushes the app context around your callback.\n\nYou usually don't need it, though. Commands registered with `@app.cli.command()` (or `bundle.cli`, `src/tessel/bundles.py:49`) get wrapped automatically by `AppGroup.command` (`src/tessel/cli.py:405`). Use `@needs_app_scope` only on plain click commands registered elsewhere. You can opt out of the wrapping with `needs_app_scope=False`.\n\n**Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo` (`src/tessel/cli.py`, `load_app()` at line 333). It locates the app via `create_app`, `--app`/`TESSEL_APP`, or `wsgi.py`/`app.py`. Access it in a command with the `pass_script_info` decorator (`src/tessel/cli.py:375`). `TesselGroup` (`src/tessel/cli.py:531`) is the top-level `tessel` CLI group that uses it.",
